   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** Kandinsky 5 Video Lite (2B) image to video: your picture becomes the first frame of a 768x512 clip, 121 frames = 5 s at 24 fps, no sound. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group): load the **Start image**. Write the **Prompt** (what moves, how the camera moves). Set **Width** / **Height** (768x512 default), **Frames** (121 = 5 s), **Steps** (50) and **Seed**.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note.\n3. **Prompt**: the negative prompt box is optional; it is empty by default.\n4. **Sampling**: euler_ancestral / beta, CFG 5, shift 5. These are the model's defaults from the official template.\n5. Press **Run**. The clip is saved by the **Result** node to `output/video/`.\n\n**What to expect:** the 5 s clip took 20 min 03 s on the test card (50 steps, CFG 5, model load included). There is no 16-step image-to-video Lite model. VRAM sat at 12.4 GB while sampling and peaked at 17.3 GB for about 20 s while decoding. On a smaller card ComfyUI should decode in tiles instead; that was not tested.\n\n**Tips**\n- The start image is centre-cropped to Width x Height. For a portrait picture swap them: Width 512, Height 768 (not tested).\n- Width and Height must be multiples of 16. The official template says to keep the area near 768x512.\n- This is the 5 s model: the authors give 5 s (121 frames) as its limit.\n\n**Why the two extra nodes after the sampler:** *Put the clean start image back* replaces the sampled first frame with your encoded picture, and *Match the first frames* sets brightness and contrast of the first 4 latent frames to those of the next 5, so the start does not stand out from the rest. Both come from the official template; the test clip showed no flash at the start.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB · 64 GB RAM · ComfyUI 0.45.3 started with --reserve-vram 12 (ComfyUI keeps its models within about 12 GB). **Not verified on a 12 GB card.**\n"
   ]
  },
