   "title": "Downloads + requirements",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Downloads + requirements\n\nClick a file name to download it. Put it in the folder shown (inside `ComfyUI/models/`).\n\n| Folder | File (click = download) | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `diffusion_models/` | [kandinsky5lite_i2v_5s.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/kandinskylab/Kandinsky-5.0-I2V-Lite-5s/resolve/main/model/kandinsky5lite_i2v_5s.safetensors) | 4.6 GB |\n| `text_encoders/` | [qwen_2.5_vl_7b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/HunyuanVideo_1.5_repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_2.5_vl_7b_fp8_scaled.safetensors) | 9.4 GB |\n| `text_encoders/` | [clip_l.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/clip_l.safetensors) | 0.25 GB |\n| `vae/` | [hunyuan_video_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Kijai/HunyuanVideo_comfy/resolve/main/hunyuan_video_vae_bf16.safetensors) | 0.49 GB |\n\nTotal: about 14.7 GB. The text encoders and VAE are the same files the Kandinsky 5 text-to-video workflow uses.\n\n**Needs ComfyUI 0.4.0 or newer** (native Kandinsky 5 support). **No custom nodes.**\n\nLicence: Kandinsky 5 Lite is MIT (commercial use allowed). Check the licences of the text encoders and VAE on their pages.\n"
   ]
